        salesDrivers: ["**Captive chrome ore**: the Ruighoek mine in South Africa (about ₹58cr, 74% owned) started production in late August 2026, with ore reaching India from Q3 FY27. Management expects the gross margin to rise from 44–45% to about 50% by the end of FY27 and keeps a **20% operating-margin target for FY28**.", "**Strontium filling up**: from about 50% use in Q1 FY27 towards 65–75% by year-end, helped by the removal of customs duty on celestite in the February 2026 budget; at 80% use it should turn 1.5–1.8 times its cost into revenue.", "**Barium growth of 15–20% in FY27**, helped by Europe's duty on Chinese barium carbonate (worth 4–5 points of margin there) and the EU trade deal removing a 6% duty.", "**New products from FY28**: DMSO, a 20,000-tonne chrome oxide green line and the chromium-metal joint venture, which also ties up chrome oxide green offtake. A 10-year take-or-pay chrome oxide green contract was described as close on the Q1 call but is not confirmed in any filing.", "**Freight and West Asia**: freight was 9–10% of revenue in Q1 and management said it could be above 20% in Q2, only partly passed on."],
